        {
          "id": "engine-stalling-is-frustrating-and-dangerous",
          "title": "Engine stalling is frustrating and dangerous",
          "description": "When your engine stalls while driving, you lose power steering and brake assistance - making the car difficult to control. In our 24,650 quote dataset, we identified five primary patterns:",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "cards",
              "cards": [
                {
                  "title": "Stalls when stopping - 30% of cases",
                  "text": "Idle air control valve or vacuum leak. Repair: £100-£400.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Stalls when stopping - 30% of cases Idle air control valve or vacuum leak. Repair: £100-£400."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Stalls when accelerating - 25% of cases",
                  "text": "Fuel pump or fuel pressure. Repair: £150-£900.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Stalls when accelerating - 25% of cases Fuel pump or fuel pressure. Repair: £150-£900."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Stalls randomly - 20% of cases",
                  "text": "Crank/cam position sensor. Repair: £100-£300.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Stalls randomly - 20% of cases Crank/cam position sensor. Repair: £100-£300."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Stalls when cold - 15% of cases",
                  "text": "Coolant temperature sensor. Repair: £80-£200.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Stalls when cold - 15% of cases Coolant temperature sensor. Repair: £80-£200."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Stalls after starting - 10% of cases",
                  "text": "Immobiliser or ECU. Repair: £100-£1,200+.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Stalls after starting - 10% of cases Immobiliser or ECU. Repair: £100-£1,200+."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The critical safety warning: If your engine stalls while driving, power steering and brake assistance are lost. The car is still controllable but requires significantly more effort to steer and stop."
            },
            {
              "type": "label",
              "text": "Common affected vehicles & engines"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "engine-stalling-is-frustrating-and-dangerous",
            "order": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "follow-this-decision-tree-to-identify-the-cause",
          "title": "Follow this decision tree to identify the cause",
          "description": "ENGINE STALLING │ ├─── When does it stall? │ │ │ ├── When stopping → Idle air valve or vacuum │ │ │ │ │ ├── EML on? → Sensor → Sensor failure │ │ │ │ │ └── No EML → Vacuum leak → Vacuum leak │ │ │ ├── When accelerating → Fuel system │ │ │ │ │ ├── Fuel pump → Fuel pump │ │ │ │ │ └── Fuel filter → Fuel filter │ │ │ ├── Random (no pattern) → Sensors │ │ │ │ │ ├── Crank sensor → Crank sensor │ │ │ │ │ └── Cam sensor → Cam sensor │ │ │ ├── When cold → Coolant temp sensor → Temp sensor │ │ │ └── After starting → Immobiliser/ECU → Immobiliser / ECU",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "label",
              "text": "Stalling types & repair costs"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
