          }
        },
        {
          "id": "safety-warning-stalling-while-driving",
          "title": "⚠️ Safety warning - stalling while driving",
          "description": "If your engine stalls while driving:",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "✅ DO:"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Keep the steering straight · Brake firmly but avoid sudden stops · Put the car in neutral and restart if safe · Pull over to a safe location"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "❌ DON'T:"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Panic - the car is still controllable · Drive far if it keeps stalling"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Loss of power steering and brake assistance: When the engine stalls, the power steering pump and brake servo stop working. The car becomes significantly harder to steer and stop. Allow extra distance for braking."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Book Diagnostic"
            },
            {
              "type": "cards",
              "cards": [
                {
                  "title": "What happens if you ignore it",
                  "text": "The safety risk: A stalling engine is a safety hazard, especially at junctions, roundabouts, or in traffic. Don't delay diagnosis.",
                  "highlight": "£100-£300 → £300-£600",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "What happens if you ignore it The cost escalates quickly Symptom Progression Cost Impact Stalls when stopping Idle valve fails completely £100-£300 → £300-£600 Stalls when accelerating Fuel pump fails £150-£900 → £400-£1,200 Stalls randomly Sensor fails, car won't start £100-£300 → £200-£600 Stalls after starting ECU fails completely £100-£400 → £300-£1,200+ The safety risk: A stalling engine is a safety hazard, especially at junctions, roundabouts, or in traffic. Don't delay diagnosis."
                },
                {
                  "title": "What to do next",
                  "text": "Step 1: Note the stalling pattern When does it stall? (stopping, accelerating, random, cold, after start). This is the most important diagnostic clue. Step 2: Check for warning lights EML on? Check Engine Light? These indicate sensor or ECU issues. Step 3: Professional diagnostic (£50-£150) A technician will read fault codes, check live data (fuel trims, sensors), test fuel pressure, and inspect idle control and vacuum system.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
